WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.298 --> 00:00:16.419
was late for supper that night, but it didn't matter.

2
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.064
While Pollyanna was out, Aunt Polly had received a telegram that her cousin had died.

3
00:00:23.084 --> 00:00:29.288
"Your aunt left right away for the funeral in Boston," Nancy explained.

4
00:00:30.272 --> 00:00:32.894
"I guess we can be glad she'll be gone for three days."

5
00:00:32.914 --> 00:00:39.859
"Oh, no, there are some things—like funerals—that you can't play the game with!

6
00:00:42.781 --> 00:00:44.302
Now let me tell you why I'm late."

7
00:00:46.423 --> 00:00:50.306
Soon Nancy was listening in amazement as Pollyanna described Mr.

8
00:00:50.346 --> 00:00:52.687
Pendleton's accident and how she'd helped him.

9
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.972
The next day Pollyanna met Jimmy by the side of the road.

10
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:06.105
She explained to the disappointed boy that the Ladies' Aiders preferred to help overseas orphans.

11
00:01:08.427 --> 00:01:09.848
He kicked a stone down the road.

12
00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:14.551
"Wouldn't it be great if somebody far away wanted me?"

13
00:01:16.973 --> 00:01:18.935
Pollyanna clapped her hands with glee.

14
00:01:18.955 --> 00:01:22.017
"I'll write to my Ladies' Aiders out West.

15
00:01:22.918 --> 00:01:25.320
They're so far away that maybe they'll want you!"

16
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:29.864
"Don't forget to say that I'll work," Jimmy reminded her.

17
00:01:32.808 --> 00:01:37.510
About a week later, Pollyanna went into the sitting room to see Aunt Polly, who was back from

18
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:41.511
Boston. "Aunt Polly, would you mind if I took Mrs.

19
00:01:41.591 --> 00:01:43.791
Snow's beef stew to someone else this week?"

20
00:01:45.312 --> 00:01:46.752
Aunt Polly looked up from her knitting.

21
00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:49.993
"What are you up to now, Pollyanna?"

22
00:01:50.013 --> 00:01:53.415
"Nothing you could possibly object to."

23
00:01:54.595 --> 00:01:57.796
Pollyanna came over and sat on the footstool near Aunt Polly's chair.

24
00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:02.847
"You let me take stew to her, so I thought you'd let me take it to him.

25
00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:07.692
You see, his broken leg will be a problem for only a few weeks.

26
00:02:09.153 --> 00:02:09.653
But Mrs.

27
00:02:09.773 --> 00:02:11.855
Snow is a lifelong invalid.

28
00:02:13.056 --> 00:02:16.239
There will be plenty of opportunities to take her stew every week."

29
00:02:16.259 --> 00:02:20.122
"Him? His broken leg?

30
00:02:20.803 --> 00:02:22.524
What on earth are you talking about?"

31
00:02:22.544 --> 00:02:26.448
"It all happened while you were away."

32
00:02:27.308 --> 00:02:30.591
Pollyanna got a faraway look in her eyes as she recalled that day.

33
00:02:30.611 --> 00:02:36.356
"I found him in the woods and had to unlock his house and call the doctor.

34
00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:40.740
Of course, then I came home, and I haven't seen him since.

35
00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.822
But Nancy was making beef stew this morning.

36
00:02:44.903 --> 00:02:46.745
And I thought it would be nice to take it to him.

37
00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:47.986
May I, Aunt Polly?"

38
00:02:48.006 --> 00:02:52.630
"Yes, I suppose so."

39
00:02:54.071 --> 00:02:55.072
Aunt Polly sighed.

40
00:02:56.628 --> 00:02:59.929
She sometimes felt worn down by conversations with Pollyanna.

41
00:02:59.949 --> 00:03:02.630
"Who did you say he was?"

42
00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.931
"Mr. John Pendleton."

43
00:03:06.392 --> 00:03:07.873
Aunt Polly sprang from her chair.

44
00:03:07.893 --> 00:03:10.033
"John Pendleton!"

45
00:03:10.053 --> 00:03:13.515
"Yes, Nancy told me his name.

46
00:03:13.935 --> 00:03:14.695
Maybe you know him?"

47
00:03:16.216 --> 00:03:18.957
Aunt Polly didn't answer but quietly sat down.

48
00:03:18.977 --> 00:03:21.338
"Do you know him?"

49
00:03:21.358 --> 00:03:23.239
"Oh, yes.

50
00:03:23.579 --> 00:03:26.040
He always smiles and speaks to me now.

51
00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.222
He's only grumpy on the outside, you know."

52
00:03:30.162 --> 00:03:31.083
Pollyanna stood up.

53
00:03:32.164 --> 00:03:33.925
"I'll go and get the stew from Nancy."

54
00:03:36.247 --> 00:03:39.409
Pollyanna was halfway across the room when Aunt Polly stopped her.

55
00:03:39.429 --> 00:03:43.151
"Wait! I've changed my mind."

56
00:03:44.112 --> 00:03:46.034
Aunt Polly's voice was suddenly stern.

57
00:03:46.054 --> 00:03:49.196
"I'd prefer that Mrs.

58
00:03:49.256 --> 00:03:51.477
Snow have that stew today as usual."

59
00:03:52.938 --> 00:03:54.860
Pollyanna's disappointment was clear.

60
00:03:56.024 --> 00:03:57.484
"But I want to bring Mr.

61
00:03:57.544 --> 00:04:00.045
Pendleton the stew before he gets better.

62
00:04:01.406 --> 00:04:04.106
And he's already had a broken leg for a whole week."

63
00:04:05.507 --> 00:04:07.527
"I do not want to send him stew."

64
00:04:08.688 --> 00:04:11.608
Aunt Polly shook her head to emphasize the "not."

65
00:04:13.709 --> 00:04:15.650
Pollyanna was not yet ready to give up.

66
00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:21.511
"I understand why you don't like him—he can be awfully grumpy sometimes.

67
00:04:22.432 --> 00:04:23.492
But how about this?

68
00:04:24.724 --> 00:04:27.005
I won't tell him that you sent the beef stew.

69
00:04:28.045 --> 00:04:29.625
I'd be glad to say it was from me."

70
00:04:32.306 --> 00:04:34.747
Aunt Polly started to shake her head again but stopped.

71
00:04:35.907 --> 00:04:40.448
She asked in a curiously quiet voice, "Does he know who you are?"

72
00:04:42.689 --> 00:04:43.669
Pollyanna sighed.

73
00:04:43.689 --> 00:04:45.550
"I don't think so.

74
00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:49.411
I told him my name once, but he never uses it."

75
00:04:49.431 --> 00:04:54.729
"Does he know where you live or that you're my niece?"

76
00:04:54.749 --> 00:04:57.270
"Oh, no.

77
00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:58.990
I never told him those things."

78
00:05:00.251 --> 00:05:04.072
For a moment there was silence as Aunt Polly stared blankly into space.

79
00:05:05.593 --> 00:05:08.994
Pollyanna waited impatiently, shifting from one foot to the other.

80
00:05:10.895 --> 00:05:12.556
At last Aunt Polly spoke.

81
00:05:12.576 --> 00:05:15.457
"Very well, you may take the stew to Mr.

82
00:05:15.477 --> 00:05:17.338
Pendleton as your own gift.

83
00:05:18.798 --> 00:05:22.480
But let's be perfectly clear about one thing: I didn't send it.

84
00:05:22.964 --> 00:05:24.306
Don't let him think that I did!"

85
00:05:26.009 --> 00:05:26.550
"Yes, ma'am.

86
00:05:26.971 --> 00:05:27.452
No, ma'am.

87
00:05:27.672 --> 00:05:28.674
Thank you, Aunt Polly!"

88
00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:31.118
Pollyanna exclaimed as she flew from the room.
